//Inheritance
Inheritance means creating a new class from an existing class so that the new class can reuse its properties and functions.

Example:

class Student {
public:
    string name;

    void study() {
        cout << "Studying";
    }
};

class CollegeStudent : public Student {
};

Here:

Student → Parent / Base class
CollegeStudent → Child / Derived class

Now:

CollegeStudent s;

s.name = "Shubham";
s.study();

CollegeStudent can use the public members inherited from Student.

Why use inheritance?

Mainly for code reuse and representing an is-a relationship.

Example:

CollegeStudent is a Student.

Simple definition:

Inheritance = mechanism where a child class acquires properties and functions of a parent class.